 qt6-base-dev, qmake6, g++
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: situc
Section: devel
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), ${misc:Depends}
Description: compiler for byte-exact data layouts
 situc compiles a schema describing a byte-exact data layout into encoders,
 decoders and checks, in C, C++, Rust and Python. Capability properties --
 in-place mutability, addressability, canonical encoding, authentication
 coverage -- are inferred statically and reported back to the schema author
 as design feedback rather than discovered at runtime.

Package: libsitu-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: C runtime for code generated by situc
 The static library and header that code generated by situc links against.
 Install this to build a C program around a situ schema.

Package: situ-edit-gui
Section: devel
Architecture: any
Depends: situc (= ${source:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: window for reading and editing a message against a situ schema
 situ-edit-gui opens a capture and a situ schema and shows every field the
 bytes hold, with what a write to each would cost; values edit where the
 schema permits it. It drives situ-edit from the situc package and holds no
 rule of its own. Built with qtty, `situ-edit-gui --tui` puts the same
 window on a terminal. A package of its own, so that situc needs Python and
 nothing else.
